WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
<b>Steak
So Tender</b>

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.910
U-Um...

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.200
I think it was over fifty years ago now...

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.460
My wife and I were still young,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.350
and we were out for a walk at night.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.760
Back then, the city wasn't 
as bright as it is today.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.250
You could see so many stars.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.340
We peeked over the edge, afraid...

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.330
And there was a baby!

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.480
That baby was Takashi!

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.480
We took him in and raised him.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.240
Y-You can't mean...

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.630
What is the director, then?!

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.620
Don't tell me you actually fell for that!

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.530
It was a joke, huh?

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.940
Sheesh... You're such a goof, kid.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.410
Black Wagyu...

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.670
This steak is so good.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.960
It's just daikon radish, though.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.180
<b><i>Planet With</i></b>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.850
Be sure you understand that vegetation
 and soil distribution are linked to weather.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.720
<b>Episode 5: Paladin Break 1</b>

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.130
Kuroi, wake up!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.400
I'm sorry, Brother!

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:52.900
Who are you calling your brother?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.470
It's the middle of class.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:55.110
Ow.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.470
Brother?

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.570
<b>Occult Research</b>

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.110
Um, Kuroi-kun, are you...

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.430
Runyah!

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.910
President!

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.170
Runyah!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.650
Runyah.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.460
There we go.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.780
Huh? Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.120
No, um...

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.530
What is that?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.530
<b>Mystery Adventure
 Super Hitoshi</b>

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.910
<b>Our Cameras Saw
 the Moment of the Explosion</b>

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.110
Magazines.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.970
They've got articles about the 
mysterious giant objects,

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.120
so I bought them with our club funds.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.290
Oh.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.440
Want to read one, Kuroi-kun?

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.250
No, I'll pass.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.460
It's got an article on the 
bombing of the Great Mountain Kitty.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.700
Great Mountain Kitty?

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.840
That big kitty cat that 
appeared out of the sky.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.550
That's what they're calling it online.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.760
That bombing...

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.810
I'm glad the town was evacuated.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.220
Yeah.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.980
But everything just froze 
when that blast went off.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.020
Is this town going to 
turn into a battlefield?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.440
Hmm. Maybe.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.990
Then they'll shut down the school,
 and we'll all split up.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:25.100
And even though we finally have enough members
 to stay open, the club will be finished.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.790
Well, I guess I can't
do anything about that...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.440
Did you say something?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.280
No...

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.750
Nezuya-senpai?

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.730
Runyah.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.390
R-Runyah?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.290
I came to bring back the books I borrowed.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.430
What's wrong, Senpai?

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.480
Is something wrong?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.930
It's weird that you're
 not being weird, I guess.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.490
And I came to say goodbye.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.650
My dad says he's shutting 
down the shop and moving.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.660
I'm going with him.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.920
My little sister's really 
scared of the massive objects,

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.010
and he's worried.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.740
And I'm sorry, Kuroi-kun,

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.040
that I won't be able to help
 you get your memories back.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.880
It's fine...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.630
What about the convenience store?

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.110
Nezuya-senpai was kind of weird today.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:30.500
Yeah.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:36.060
He was acting normal,
 but also kind of... weak.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:36.690
Yeah.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.610
No way, that thing doesn't kill you.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.980
Runyah!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.790
Runyah.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.780
But something in him died.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.450
What?

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.740
Nothing.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.370
Hey, was your brother like Nezuya-senpai?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.540
Not at all.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.500
I knew it.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.610
Your memories!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.060
What's that "oops" face supposed to mean?

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.760
It wasn't important enough to bring up.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.600
It looked less like you didn't 
think it was important,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.100
and more like you wanted to keep it a secret.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.510
Wh-Why would you think that?

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.960
And those memories have something 
to do with the massive objects

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.670
that have appeared lately?

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.170
N-N-Nope!

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.440
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Why?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.090
Because when the first one showed up,

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.420
you were excited to see a real UFO,

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.360
but after that, you've been 
acting really normal.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.740
You've been more into 
UMA books than UFO books.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:40.670
And when you saw the magazine cover today,
 you just looked sick of it.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.790
Well? Am I right?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.500
Tell me!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.320
Um, I'll be going!

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.170
Bye!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.300
Wait!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.180
I-I'm sorry!

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:57.110
Kuroi-kun, wait!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.470
Ow...

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:06.730
Um, I'm sorry.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:08.740
I'm sorry...

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.200
For being so nosy just to 
satisfy my own curiosity.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.200
You need to keep it a secret, right?

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.710
But I...

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.430
I'm really sorry.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:25.030
I was afraid you'd start 
skipping school again.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.300
That's why I tackled you.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:33.760
It's not something I need to keep a secret.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.690
Well, um...

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.980
If I told you I was an alien, 
would you believe it?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.440
I don't know.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.760
I look just like a human because we 
both developed from the same race,

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.640
and it's one that's very common 
in the universe or something.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:54.030
It's too big to take in.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.490
Normally, you wouldn't believe that, yeah?

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.080
Is it better if I don't?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.190
No...

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:05.790
It doesn't matter.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.040
There was no need for me to say it,

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.810
and there's no need to make you believe it.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.760
That's why I didn't say anything before.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:16.370
I didn't think you'd connect 
it to the spaceships.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:19.470
So I panicked and just made things worse.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.930
Those are spaceships?

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.360
Also, we weren't the ones 
who attacked the town.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.650
I want you to believe that.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.910
It's... all true.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.080
It's all a lie.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.080
You're such a goof, believing all that...

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.210
Okay. I'll pretend that's how it is.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.890
Bye.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.140
I'll be going.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:56.840
Wait.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.680
Make sure you come to school tomorrow.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.640
Okay, got it. I will.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.130
Thank you!

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.540
I'm sorry. Thank you.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.410
No, it's not your fault...

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.700
I'm sorry, I guess.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.360
Thanks.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.170
I'm sorry!

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.830
No, it's not your fault.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.040
I'm sorry, I guess.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:24.370
Thanks.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:28.270
Also, I don't think any boy 
your age says "goof."

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:29.810
Yeah?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.350
See you later.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:35.590
Okay, bye.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.590
Oh, one last thing.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:44.310
Thank you for protecting the town!

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:45.380
Bye!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.730
I-I didn't...

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.020
You did!

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.350
When did you get here?

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.020
You just did.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:57.950
You protected the town when the 
dragon went out of control.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.060
She doesn't think of you 
as an invader, does she?

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.630
I protected the town?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:28.810
There it is!

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.610
Wh-What the hell is that?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.610
<b>Universe</b>

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.560
A turtle and some elephants are
holding up a bowl of rice?

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.570
<b>Universe</b>

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.320
And then a snake passed 
out inside the rice? What?

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.650
The proper shape of the world, yes.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.080
What is?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.780
To eat is to live.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.950
And life is the world itself.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.020
In other words, food is the world.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.540
And the world is food.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.640
That's deep... I guess?

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.630
I'm sorry. I don't get it.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:00.800
By the way, are you sure you didn't want 
to leave Paladin along with Benika-chan?

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:06.280
If I do, you'll have to 
fight on your own, right?

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.880
You're such a good kid.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.710
<i>Look! Another huge mysterious 
object has appeared,</i>

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:17.580
<i>and is approaching the coast!</i>

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.900
<b>Breaking News: Huge Mysterious Object Appears Again</b>

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:20.250
<i>All locals are asked to evacuate immediately!</i>

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.490
<i>Kuroi-kun...</i>

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.780
Okay, off we go.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:35.880
<b>Another Huge Mysterious Object Appears Again
It appears to be closing in on Soramisaka City's coast</b>

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.980
<i>The nature of these huge 
creatures is still unknown,</i>

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:42.590
<i>along with that of the warriors 
of light who oppose it.</i>

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.720
Something's flying at us.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.490
Something?

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.770
R-Rice grains?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:55.940
Rice?!

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.690
Whoa, look out!

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.870
If it had been meat,
 I would've eaten the hit.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.320
What are you talking about?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.950
The Sealing Faction's got the worst 
taste in spaceships, as usual.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.810
The Earth's got just two people, huh?

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:14.220
And the sealing faction has 
brought out a powerful seal.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.000
The Earthlings are at a big disadvantage.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.420
That's what Sensei says.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:25.000
The Sealing Faction may 
intend to end things here.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.760
End things?

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:29.920
To wipe out any last human resistance,

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.850
and finish the sealing of humanity.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.460
The sealing of humanity?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.440
Runyah!

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:39.940
Runyah.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:43.030
I saw somebody the Sealing Faction got.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.370
He looked like he'd grown up.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.330
But he also looked... like the fire 
had gone out in his eyes.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.030
What is that, exactly?

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.340
So that's its weak point?

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.710
Please head inside from there.

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.050
Be careful.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.620
<i>Right. I'll leave the rest to you.</i>

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.050
Okay! G-Good luck!

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:15.080
The sealing device gives people 
a variety of gentle dreams.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.120
Their wishes and ambitions coming true...

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.860
A sense of fulfillment...

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.720
Welcome home!

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.630
We've been waiting for you.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:42.590
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:48.260
These gentle dreams fill 
the gaps in the heart.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:54.480
Their price is that they steal 
the heart's hunger, and its hope.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.600
What happens if you lose that?

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.900
People stop moving forward.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.560
Yum, yum! Give me more!

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:07.530
The sealing device doesn't hurt anyone.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:12.400
But it quietly puts out the 
fire in someone's heart.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.460
Are you done yet, grandpa?

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:23.630
That was fun.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:27.090
Okay, time to head out.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:35.950
Takezo-san...

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:40.630
Eiko!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.030
What, are you here to stop me, too?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.150
Haven't you done enough?

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:53.620
I'm the only one left in the 
Grand Whatsit that Takashi founded.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:57.580
Yosuke's heart already isn't in it.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.470
<i>I knew he didn't have it 
in him to be a leader.</i>

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.720
<i>That's why I have to be 
his ally until the end.</i>

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.340
I see.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.680
Don't laugh and tell me I'm 
too old not to let my kid go.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.250
No.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.620
I'm glad to have such a good husband.

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.630
Goodbye.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.690
See you around, Eiko!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.190
Come get me when I'm dead!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:32.230
Damn you, Nebula. That was a 
lot harder than the other one.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.540
<b>"You have nothing to regret."</b>

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.100
I don't need your advice, alien!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:58.350
The snake...

00:15:58.670 --> 00:15:59.620
Why?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.190
You destroyed the core, right?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:07.060
Oh, no... So that part was a separate unit?

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.310
It got past us!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.450
It's coming toward us!

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:16.830
Tch! If we get inside the 
enemy's field unprotected...

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.390
The massive object is heading this way!

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:22.070
It's about to reach the town!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.180
Isn't it going really fast?

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.780
It's fast! Run! Run!

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:26.500
Quickly!

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:27.720
It's so fast!

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:28.460
I can't catch up!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.550
No! It's going to make land!

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:42.480
What is that?

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:47.440
A flash of light suddenly appeared and 
stopped the massive object in its tracks!

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.150
<b>Breaking News: Huge Mysterious Object Appears Again</b>

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:50.610
<i>Is it one of the warriors of light 
who were fighting the others?</i>

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.570
That must be Kuroi-kun.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:56.660
A Nebula Soldier?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:58.280
Why?

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.340
The Nebula Soldier is fighting 
the Nebula Weapon.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:04.750
So it was true after all?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.960
The Sealing Faction and 
the Pacifist Faction...

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.420
Nebula is split down the middle internally!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:15.590
<i>You used Cat Doping again.</i>

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.370
<i>Expect a hangover tomorrow.</i>

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.220
<i>That's what Sensei says.</i>

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.800
I needed to fly. I didn't have a choice.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:23.950
Sorry, Nozo-san.

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:25.530
I'll be skipping school tomorrow.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.030
It's looking at us.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.930
Giga Cat Blade!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:41.660
Come on!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:54.720
Wow, it's a heck of a lot 
slower than that dragon.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.930
A single attack?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:00.020
The claws of the newly-arrived 
warrior of light

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:01.900
took out the massive object 
with a single attack.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.640
The town...

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.520
The town is saved!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.270
It defeated it without 
going inside the core?!

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:16.610
Do its attacks work because 
it's also a Nebula Weapon?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.270
The Nebula Soldier defeated 
the Nebula Weapon?

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:22.530
So it was true?

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.370
Huh? Old man!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.960
Reconstructing Psychokinetic Photon Armor!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.080
Come forth, my sword!

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.630
That was close.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:40.970
Not bad.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.020
Damn it!

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:42.930
I let my guard down!

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:43.860
Old man!

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:44.930
He didn't hesitate at all?!

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:47.890
Can you hear me, little Nebula kid?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.600
We're doing the same thing 
as usual today, right?

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:50.810
Fighting for my bottle.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:54.710
I figured with your speed, I couldn't escape.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:56.990
So I hit first.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.530
But you don't mind, do you?

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.660
Yeah, no complaints here.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.240
Let's get right to fighting!

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:06.210
Just what I wanted to hear!

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.920
Be careful, Soya!

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.380
That sword is dangerous!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.420
Make absolutely sure it doesn't hit you!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.550
That's what Sensei says!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:16.850
Right.

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:18.090
I know.

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:21.510
Old man...

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.290
Is that the old man?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.110
So you were hiding your true 
power after all, you old geezer.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.900
Let me ask you a question.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.570
Why did you protect the town?

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:39.460
No reason.

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.030
I just did it on Sensei and Ginko's orders.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:46.140
That was not the blade of 
someone acting under orders.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.980
I'm asking the person inside.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.250
Who is your enemy, and who is your ally?

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:51.840
I...

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:57.530
I'm the friend of those I want to befriend,

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.800
and the enemy of those I want to defeat!

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.010
A beast, then.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.970
Yes, a beast.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.690
<i>I want courage...</i>

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:13.380
<i>The courage to jump right at that thing!</i>

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.610
<i>Brother!</i>

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:26.450
Lend me your power, Eiko!

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:39.990
Director?

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:41.720
What is it, Shiraishi-kun?

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.430
Why call me out to the 
roof at a time like this?

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.890
The preparations have been completed.

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:49.580
Preparations?

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:52.150
Generalissimo, go ahead.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:03.640
"The rental period on my secretary 
is up, Takashi Ryuzoji."

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:05.570
So says the Generalissimo.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:09.390
Oh? So you're Nebula's leader?

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:12.830
So you did realize I work for Nebula?

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:17.540
Your hypnosis won't work 
on me, Shiraishi-kun.

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:22.060
Though it seems that nobody but 
Takatori-kun had any doubts.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:26.320
"Nobody will interrupt us here."

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:28.590
"It's the perfect day for a final battle."

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.520
So says the Generalissimo.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:31.620
A final battle?

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:32.850
Very well.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.440
There's lots I'd like to ask you...

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:39.100
But I've no objections to 
deciding Earth's fate here.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:42.900
Takashi Ryuzoji, prepare to die!

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.530
Shiraishi-kun, what just 
happened to your clothes?

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:57.630
Well, whatever.

00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:58.480
Here I go!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
<b><i>To Be Continued</i></b>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.140
<b><i>Next Time
Paladin Break 2</i></b>

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:45.140
"Paladin Break 2."
